&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About NetEase Games:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a leading internet technology company based in China, NetEase, Inc. (NASDAQ: NTES and HKEX:9999, “NetEase”) provides premium online services centered around content creation. With extensive offerings across its expanding gaming ecosystem, the Company develops and operates some of China’s most popular and longest-running mobile and PC games. Powered by industry-leading in-house R&amp;amp;D capabilities in China and globally, NetEase creates superior gaming experiences, inspires players, and passionately delivers value for its thriving community worldwide. By infusing play with culture and education with technology, NetEase transforms gaming into a meaningful vehicle to build a more entertaining and enlightened world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NetEase’s ESG initiatives are among the best in the global media and entertainment industry, earning it a distinction as one of the S&amp;amp;P Global Industry Movers and an “A” rating from MSCI. For more information, please visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://ir.netease.com/&quot;&gt;http://ir.netease.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead the design and execution of performance animation for key story sequences and interactive cinematics, overseeing facial performances, dialogue scenes, and action-driven performances to ensure emotional authenticity and cinematic quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate closely with Art, Design, and Engineering teams to establish and maintain production pipelines and quality standards for performance animation, ensuring consistency in character emotions and visual storytelling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Define production guidelines and animation standards for facial performances, dialogue scenes, and character acting, driving scalable and efficient content creation workflows while continuously improving quality and productivity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leverage experience from the film and game industries to optimize motion capture and keyframe animation pipelines, solve technical challenges, and enhance the overall quality and expressiveness of character performances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or above in Animation, Film, Directing, Digital Media Arts, or related disciplines preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;3+ years of experience as an Animation Director, Action Director, Performance Animator, or related role in the film or game industry. Candidates must provide portfolio examples demonstrating both action-oriented and subtle dramatic performances.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deep understanding of cinematic language, character acting, and emotional storytelling. Ability to independently deliver high-quality performances ranging from facial animation and dialogue scenes to action-driven sequences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proficiency in motion capture data processing, keyframe animation, and in-engine performance integration. Ability to solve technical challenges throughout the animation production pipeline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration and communication skills, with the ability to work effectively with Art, Design, and Engineering teams to drive production standards and pipeline execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong industrialized production mindset. Experience establishing animation standards, optimizing workflows, and improving team-wide delivery quality is highly preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced production environment. Prior experience in film production studios or cinematic teams is a plus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;article&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About NetEaseGames:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a leading internet technology company based in China, NetEase, Inc. (NASDAQ: NTES and HKEX:9999, “NetEase”) provides premium online services centered around content creation. With extensive offerings across its expanding gaming ecosystem, the Company develops and operates some of China’s most popular and longest-running mobile and PC games. Powered by industry-leading in-house R&amp;amp;D capabilities in China andglobally, NetEase creates superior gaming experiences, inspires players, and passionately delivers value for its thriving community worldwide. By infusing play with culture and education with technology, NetEase transforms gaming intoa meaningful vehicle to build a more entertaining and enlightened world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NetEase’s ESG initiatives are among the best in the global media and entertainment industry, earning it adistinction as one of the S&amp;amp;P Global Industry Movers and an “A” rating from MSCI. For more information, please visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://ir.netease.com/&quot;&gt;http://ir.netease.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for planning and operating overseas gaming communities, developing and executing community strategies and objectives based on the product&#39;s market strategy and game version schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the promotional scheduling, publishing, and performance evaluation of game version content within the community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously optimize Discord community functions based on player needs and preferences, ensuring the community meets player needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect and report on player feedback and sentiment; Monitor competing products and new releases in the genre.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or above, with proficiencyin English as a working language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in operating large overseas gaming communities (Discord), with proven operational expertise in community and platform management, capable of developing and implementing community strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep gaming experience with overseas titles; familiar with shooter/competitive game genres, with clear insights into player demographics and the gaming industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and execution skills, collaborative team spirit, and a sense of responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Chinese is required for this position, as daily communication and collaboration with game development team based in China are essential to the responsibilities of the position.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;190&quot; data-end=&quot;199&quot;&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; All UK-based positions are &lt;strong data-start=&quot;227&quot; data-end=&quot;260&quot;&gt;eligible for visa sponsorship&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/article&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-Driven Growth Video/Image Content Production: Proficiently use mainstream AI video/image generation models and editing tools to independently handle creative ideation, asset generation, and post-production (editing, motion graphics, audio-visual compositing, etc.) for growth ad videos and marketing images. Produce ad creatives that balance aesthetic quality and conversion effectiveness to support the content needs of overseas growth business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build an AI Asset Production System: Develop an automated visual asset production pipeline based on AI Agents, covering core scenarios such as ad video generation and editing, marketing image generation and editing, and website page design. Drive the stable implementation of AI-driven large-scale asset production in growth business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Abstract High-Conversion Strategies: Deeply deconstruct the visual language of high-converting ad videos, websites, and image assets — including narrative pacing, camera language, opening hooks, audio-visual synergy, as well as layout, color, composition, and visual hierarchy — and translate them into reusable prompt strategies and Agent workflows to continuously improve asset conversion efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Asset Performance Evaluation System: Establish a quantitative evaluation system that covers both &quot;content quality&quot; and &quot;ad delivery performance&quot;. Provide quality scores and optimization suggestions through multi-dimensional assessment, and take ownership of the final output quality of growth assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scaled Quality Assurance: Address issues in the generation pipeline such as style inconsistency, brand deviation, character and visual coherence, and localization adaptation. Design effective strategies to ensure the stability and usability of batch-produced content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Team Collaboration: Integrate resources from algorithms (prompt/model application), design (aesthetic control), and operations (feedback iteration) to drive efficient execution of growth projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Background: Bachelor’s degree or above; candidates with backgrounds in film/TV production, digital media art, animation, visual communication, or advertising design are preferred. 5+ years of experience in ad video design, internet visual design, or overseas growth asset design; 2+ years of hands-on experience in AI-driven design, automated asset production, or Agent products. Experience in feed/short-video ad creative design, or overseas growth design for tool/content products is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI Application Capability: Deep understanding of the capabilities and boundaries of mainstream image/video generation foundation models and Agent tools. Ability to flexibly leverage foundation models, Agents, and other tools to solve business problems. Proven experience in video/image model orchestration and automated workflow construction is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business Acumen: Familiarity with overseas growth ad creative workflows (in-feed video ads, TikTok/YouTube/Meta ad assets, landing page and campaign page visuals, etc.). Strong ability to deconstruct narrative pacing, camera language, audio-visual synergy, layout composition, color systems, visual hierarchy, and image-copy coordination. Excellent aesthetic perception and visual language understanding, with awareness of overseas localized aesthetic differences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systematic Logic Capability: Strong product abstraction ability to translate complex growth requirements into clear technical solutions and executable roadmap planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Sensitivity: Skilled at problem attribution through data analysis. Able to independently analyze underlying issues in production pipelines and conversion performance and propose solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry Insight: Continuously track technology and product advances in image/video generation, design Agents, and intelligent workflows. Keenly assess how technological boundaries can expand growth efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About NetEaseGames:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a leading internet technology company based in China, NetEase, Inc. (NASDAQ: NTES and HKEX:9999, “NetEase”)provides premium online services centered around content creation. With extensive offerings across its expanding gaming ecosystem, the Company develops and operates some of China’s most popular and longest-running mobile and PC games. Powered by industry-leading in-house R&amp;amp;D capabilities in China and globally, NetEase creates superior gaming experiences, inspires players, and passionately delivers value for its thriving community worldwide. By infusing play with culture and education with technology, NetEase transforms gaming into meaningful vehicle to build a more entertaining and enlightened world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NetEase’s ESG initiatives are among the best in the global media and entertainment industry, earning it a distinction as one of the S&amp;amp;P Global Industry Movers and an “A” rating from MSCI. For more information, please visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://ir.netease.com/&quot;&gt;http://ir.netease.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for the planning and execution of esports tournaments for shooting game products. Based on product highlights, features, and release timelines, designing online and offline tournament operation plans, building the official and third-party tournament ecosystem from the ground up, and ensuring effective implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage tournament partnership ecosystems, create diverse tournament content gameplay and third-party platform events to amplify game visibility and engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee tournament ecosystem operations, including scouting and maintaining relationships with professional players in official tournaments, executing incentive and operational policies, supporting high-quality tournament content and nurturing potential KOLs, as well as managing hot-topic activations at key milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate tournament planning, marketing strategies, and ecosystem operations, coordinating resources to achieve KPIs. Continuously track and analyze tournament data, user feedback, and market dynamics to iterate and optimize strategies for maximum project impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or above, with 2+ years of experience in esports tournament operations. Prior experience in esports operation or successful execution of esports events is preferred; experience with shooting game tournaments is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with one or multiple mainstream esports event systems in the market, and well-acquainted with the ecosystem and operational strategies of community tournaments and self-organized competitions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth understanding of competitive gaming communities, ecosystems, tournament structures, and player dynamic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in English, able to use it as a working language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Chinese is required for this position, as daily communication and collaboration with game development team based in China are essential to the responsibilities of the position.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;190&quot; data-end=&quot;199&quot;&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; All UK-based positions are &lt;strong data-start=&quot;227&quot; data-end=&quot;260&quot;&gt;eligible for visa sponsorship&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About NetEase Games:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a leading internet technology company based in China, NetEase, Inc. (NASDAQ: NTES and HKEX:9999, “NetEase”) provides premium online services centered around content creation. With extensive offerings across its expanding gaming ecosystem, the Company develops and operates some of China’s most popular and longest-running mobile and PC games. Powered by industry-leading in-house R&amp;amp;D capabilities in China and globally, NetEase creates superior gaming experiences, inspires players, and passionately delivers value for its thriving community worldwide. By infusing play with culture and education with technology, NetEase transforms gaming into a meaningful vehicle to build a more entertaining and enlightened world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NetEase’s ESG initiatives are among the best in the global media and entertainment industry, earning it a distinction as one of the S&amp;amp;P Global Industry Movers and an “A” rating from MSCI. For more information, please visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://ir.netease.com/&quot;&gt;http://ir.netease.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create high-quality first-person and third-person weapon and tactical animations, including reloads, slides, vaults, weapon inspections, and other combat-related actions, ensuring realistic feel and smooth gameplay pacing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish quality standards and production guidelines for realistic animation. Define asset output specifications and coordinate outsourced animation production to maintain consistent styles across multiple characters and weapon types.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with engineers and Technical Animators to optimize hit reactions, camera shake, and physics-driven accessories, using animation details to enhance combat feedback and tactical immersion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the design of innovative interaction animations, such as dynamic weapon inspections with different attachments, posture variations under different load conditions, and terrain-adaptive traversal animations to enrich battlefield experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements：&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;true&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;5+ years of professional 3D animation experience, including at least 3 years on FPS or TPS projects. Experience shipping realistic military shooters or survival shooters is preferred. Proficiency with 3ds Max, Maya, MotionBuilder, and deep knowledge of Unreal Engine 5 animation systems or comparable engines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Strong understanding of body mechanics, firearm operation, and tactical movements. Ability to differentiate weapon handling styles through subtle timing and motion details. Motion capture experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with first-person weapon sway systems. Experience with procedural animation or implementing facial capture workflows is preferred. Being a dedicated player of realistic shooters such as Arena Breakout: Infinite, Escape from Tarkov, or similar titles is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: left;&quot;&gt;Strong attention to realistic gameplay feel and animation details, with the ability to balance visual quality and runtime performance. Comfortable with iterative development and repeated polish. Excellent cross-functional communication skills and a collaborative mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NetEase, Inc. (Nasdaq: NTES and HKEX: 9999) is a global powerhouse in the Internet and video game industry, with a market capitalization of $70+ billion and more than 25,000 employees worldwide. The NetEase group encompasses a range of innovative businesses centered around content creation, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;NetEase Games&lt;/em&gt;, one of the largest and most renowned game developers worldwide by size, revenue and game offerings. Over the years, NetEase Games has focused on developing high quality content and providing the best experience for gamers around the world;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Youdao &lt;/em&gt;(NYSE: DAO), a majority-controlled subsidiary of NetEase, Inc. and China’s leading technology-focused intelligent learning company;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Cloud Music &lt;/em&gt;(HKEX: 9899), a majority-controlled subsidiary of NetEase, Inc. and China’s leading online music content community;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Yanxuan&lt;/em&gt;, NetEase’s private label consumer lifestyle brand; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Other innovative businesses&lt;/em&gt;, including, among others, an online payment platform and to-B technology solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About this Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is your chance to have a critical impact at a dynamic gaming company in the midst of an exciting globalization journey. You&#39;ll be joining the Group International Legal Department which oversees legal matters for the NetEase group and coordinates with the legal teams within each division of the group.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a talented Group Litigation &amp;amp; Disputes Counsel to manage and help drive the resolution of the NetEase group’s litigation, arbitration and other disputes worldwide, with a focus on U.S. litigation, Hong Kong-seated arbitration and other cross-border disputes involving our businesses in North America, APAC and Europe, while also managing internal investigation matters as they arise. In this role, you will collaborate closely with HR, business departments, Internal Audit, Finance and other legal team members to manage risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position will report to the General Counsel of NetEase, Inc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NetEase operates in multiple countries globally, and this role is primarily responsible for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overseeing and managing a broad portfolio of global disputes, including U.S. litigation, Hong Kong-seated arbitration and other cross-border commercial, IP, employment, regulatory and platform-related disputes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing and executing litigation and arbitration strategy, including early case assessments, claims and defenses, forum and procedural strategy, discovery and evidence strategy, settlement options and business-risk analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing outside counsel to deliver business-oriented outcomes, including selecting and supervising counsel across diverse jurisdictions, setting clear scope, strategy, staffing and budget expectations, managing legal costs against approved budgets and billing guidelines, and ensuring strategies are pragmatic, commercially focused and aligned with the Company’s objectives and risk tolerance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing dispute resolution and regulatory inquiries before and after outside counsel engagement, including responding to demand letters, threatened claims, subpoenas and regulatory requests, conducting settlement negotiations, and working with regulators and law enforcement as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overseeing and conducting legally privileged investigations as they arise, which includes defining scope, reviewing documentation, developing investigative plans, notifying appropriate personnel, conducting interviews, compiling investigation status and reports, recommending and implementing proper remedial measures and concluding matters appropriately.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing on-site support globally to different business units on litigation, arbitration, regulatory inquiries and internal investigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overseeing legal holds, document preservation, fact development, witness preparation, discovery and privilege issues, and ensuring proper documentation and record-keeping across litigation, arbitration and investigation matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proposing solutions and improvements to current processes, including the litigation and case-management processes, whistleblowing processes, anti-bribery and corruption program, and supplier/vendor due diligence processes, with a focus on addressing root causes and supporting compliance with local laws and regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partnering with HR, business managers and legal and compliance teams to drive best practices globally with regards to enforcement of compliance policies, internal investigations and regulatory reporting via the creation, implementation and monitoring and testing of policies, strategies and processes that build a culture of integrity and compliance across geographies in a complex business environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creating lessons learned materials and providing post-matter training to business and functional departments based on matters handled.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring the General Counsel and Company’s executive leadership have clear and timely visibility into material disputes and litigation trends in the jurisdictions in which NetEase operates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Admitted and licensed attorney in U.S., Hong Kong, Singapore or another major common-law jurisdiction with 8+ years relevant post-qualification experience working in well-regarded law firms and/or in-house legal teams; in-house experience preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience working with a variety of international businesses, corporate structures and corporate governance environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience managing litigation, arbitration and other dispute resolution across jurisdictions (U.S. litigation and/or Hong Kong-seated or international arbitration experience required), with working knowledge of internal investigations and related policies, processes and industry best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with the flexibility and cultural sensitivity to connect with colleagues across the globe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership abilities, including the ability to influence and drive change within the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to make informed decisions in complex situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of integrity, discretion, and confidentiality in handling sensitive employee and business information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in managing outside counsel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with a geographically dispersed team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong advocacy skills and a proven ability to positively influence decision-makers in contentious, sensitive or challenging situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel to multiple jurisdictions to manage disputes and conduct internal investigations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Mandarin Chinese is a significant plus as this role involves regular collaboration with regional teams and Mandarin speaking stakeholders, including counterparts based in China&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Location: &lt;/strong&gt;Hong Kong, Singapore or another Asia-Pacific hub; U.S., Canada or other locations considered for exceptional candidates&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fair Employment Practices&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;At NetEase, we are committed to fair employment practices. We welcome applications from all individuals, irrespective of age, gender, race, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company：&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NetEase, Inc. (Nasdaq: NTES and HKEX: 9999) is a global powerhouse in the Internet and online game industry, with a market capitalization of $80+ billion and more than 25,000 employees worldwide. The NetEase group encompasses a range of innovative businesses centered around content creation, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;NetEase&lt;/em&gt; Games, one of the largest and most renowned game developers worldwide by size, revenue and game offerings. Over the years, NetEase Games has focused on developing high quality content and providing the best experience for gamers around the world;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Youdao &lt;/em&gt;(NYSE: DAO), a majority-controlled subsidiary of NetEase, Inc. and China’s leading technology-focused intelligent learning company;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Cloud Music &lt;/em&gt;(HKEX: 9899), a majority-controlled subsidiary of NetEase, Inc. and China’s leading online music content community;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Yanxuan&lt;/em&gt;, NetEase’s private label consumer lifestyle brand; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Other innovative businesses&lt;/em&gt;, including, among others, an online payment platform and to-B AI technology solutions provider.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About this Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a mid-level&lt;strong&gt; Group Privacy Legal Counsel&lt;/strong&gt; with 4–8 years of experience to join our legal team. You will manage global privacy compliance, mitigate data risks, and support cross-functional teams on privacy-by-design initiatives, reporting to NetEase’s Head of Privacy &amp;amp; Data Protection. You will also support cybersecurity risk management and compliance with emerging AI regulations and related matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is part of the Group International Legal department which oversees legal matters for the NetEase group (ex-China) and coordinates with the legal teams within each division of the group.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities Include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance Management&lt;/strong&gt;: Maintain and update global privacy policies, notices, and internal frameworks for our global business units, including online games, music streaming, e-commerce, e-sports, intelligent learning, and others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Counseling&lt;/strong&gt;: Work with product and engineering teams to implement privacy-by-design and privacy-by-default and responsible AI principles into product lifecycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk Assessments&lt;/strong&gt;: Provide legal guidance on cross-border data transfers and data localization requirements and conduct, review, and document Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contract Management&lt;/strong&gt;: Draft, negotiate, and review Data Processing Agreements (DPAs) as well as the data privacy-related provisions in a wide range of commercial agreements with third parties, including IP licensing and software co-development agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incident Response&lt;/strong&gt;: Investigate potential data/cybersecurity incidents and manage regulatory notification obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee Training&lt;/strong&gt;: Design and deliver privacy and AI awareness training across global offices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Monitoring&lt;/strong&gt;: Track emerging privacy and AI laws (e.g., GDPR, CCPA/CPRA, EU AI Act, EU Digital Services Act, local regulations) and update frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Outside Counsel&lt;/strong&gt;: Collaborate and coordinate with outside counsel across various jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Other&lt;/strong&gt;: Take on other relevant duties as assigned and commensurate with your ability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualification: &lt;/strong&gt;Qualified lawyer in the U.S., Hong Kong, Singapore, UK and/or Canada.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience: &lt;/strong&gt;4 to 8 years of legal practice focused on privacy and data protection, cybersecurity and emerging technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry Background: &lt;/strong&gt;Mix of major law firm training and in-house corporate experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tech Literacy: &lt;/strong&gt;Understanding of data flows and mapping, cloud computing, and modern IT architecture, and familiarity or interest in the interactive entertainment industry in general.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Languages:&lt;/strong&gt; Fluency in English and Mandarin Chinese. This role supports business operations across multiple regions and business units and requires frequent collaboration with Mandarin-speaking stakeholders and cross-functional teams at NetEase&#39;s headquarters in China.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;Preferably Hong Kong or Singapore.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Certifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Certifications&lt;/strong&gt;: CIPP/E, CIPP/US, or CIPM designations are highly desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Self-starter&lt;/strong&gt;: Demonstrates high self-initiative and can work with teams to drive projects to pragmatic solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication&lt;/strong&gt;: Ability to translate complex legal requirements into actionable business advice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dynamic Work Environment&lt;/strong&gt;: Growth mindset that can thrive in a dynamic, cross-border environment, while working effectively across different disciplines, cultures, and time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fair Employment Practices&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;At NetEase, we are committed to fair employment practices. We welcome applications from all individuals, irrespective of age, gender, race, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NetEase, Inc. (Nasdaq: NTES and HKEX: 9999) is a global powerhouse in the Internet and video game industry, with a market capitalization of $70+ billion and more than 25,000 employees worldwide. The NetEase group encompasses a range of innovative businesses centered around content creation, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;NetEase Games&lt;/em&gt;, one of the largest and most renowned game developers worldwide by size, revenue and game offerings. Over the years, NetEase Games has focused on developing high quality content and providing the best experience for gamers around the world;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Youdao &lt;/em&gt;(NYSE: DAO), a majority-controlled subsidiary of NetEase, Inc. and China’s leading technology-focused intelligent learning company;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Cloud Music &lt;/em&gt;(HKEX: 9899), a majority-controlled subsidiary of NetEase, Inc. and China’s leading online music content community;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Yanxuan&lt;/em&gt;, NetEase’s private label consumer lifestyle brand; and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Other innovative businesses&lt;/em&gt;, including, among others, an online payment platform and to-B technology solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About this Role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is your chance to have a critical impact at a dynamic gaming company in the midst of an exciting globalization journey. You&#39;ll be joining the Group International Legal Department which oversees legal matters for the NetEase group and coordinates with the legal teams within each division of the group.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a talented Group Transactional and Commercial Counsel.&amp;nbsp; In this leadership role, you will be advising on a dynamic range of M&amp;amp;A, investments and divestments across multiple jurisdictions, and technology, media and telecom and general commercial matters at the highest international standards, including licensing, outsourcing, software technology development and professional services agreements, innovative FinTech projects, regulatory matters and cross-border technology transfers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position will report to the General Counsel of NetEase, Inc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NetEase operates in multiple countries globally, and this role is primarily responsible for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Corporate Transactions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead deal execution on a wide range of corporate transactions, including structuring, drafting, and negotiating transaction documents for acquisitions, disposals, minority investments, fund investments, financing transactions and joint ventures across multiple jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess and advise senior stakeholders on legal, regulatory, and commercial risks relating to corporate transactions.&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate regulatory approvals including antitrust, foreign investment clearances, and securities law requirements across multiple jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with legal team to provide end-to-end transaction support, including structuring, due diligence, drafting, negotiation, and completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate closely with internal business teams (e.g., senior management of business units and the NetEase group, business development, finance, tax, etc.) on all aspects of transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide legal support on post-transaction monitoring and corporate governance matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial Contract Management &amp;amp; TMT Advisory&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, review, and negotiate a variety of TMT and other commercial agreements for the NetEase group and individual business units across multiple jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide thought leadership regarding the legal and regulatory aspects of projects involving cutting-edge technologies such as Web3, blockchain, AI, tokenization, online payment systems, AI, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on TMT related policies and procedures, including terms of use and custody and trust arrangements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep up-to-date with the most recent technology legal and business developments and continue to develop relevant knowledge within the sectors in which the NetEase group operates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support NetEase group&#39;s corporate functions (finance, tax, procurement, IT, corporate secretarial, corporate M&amp;amp;A/ JV, global investments, HR, treasury and others), including daily contract reviews, in-house advisory and commercial disputes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish contract standards and templates to streamline the review process for everyday commercial agreements across business units.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and mentor a high-performing team of legal counsel, fostering a collaborative, business-oriented legal culture, and work closely with other legal specialists within the NetEase group.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide training to the wider legal &amp;amp; internal control functions, business partners and executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Select, manage and coordinate external counsel and advisors across different jurisdictions to ensure high-quality, cost-effective representation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to bridge international deals using high-level Mandarin and English language skills to review and negotiate bilingual transaction and commercial documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Admitted and licensed attorney in U.S., Hong Kong, Singapore or another major common-law jurisdiction with 8+ years relevant post-qualification experience working in well-regarded law firms and/or in-house legal teams; in-house experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead, manage and motivate team members located in multiple jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter and able to navigate various stakeholders/ businesses operating in different sectors and jurisdictions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent transactional training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise with TMT laws, regulations and industry best practices across different regions, including an understanding of emerging trends such as in the areas of FinTech/blockchain, money transmission, AI, online game regulation and digital infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong drafting, negotiating and problem-solving skills and the ability to manage complex issues and deal structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent leadership and communication skills, with the flexibility and cultural sensitivity to bring different perspectives together and work through competing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership abilities, including the ability to influence and drive change within the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to make informed decisions in complex situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced in managing outside counsel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with a geographically dispersed team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-level proficiency in Mandarin Chinese and English is a must.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Location: &lt;/strong&gt;Hong Kong, Singapore or another Asia-Pacific hub; U.S., Canada or other locations considered for exceptional candidates.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fair Employment Practices&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;At NetEase, we are committed to fair employment practices. We welcome applications from all individuals, irrespective of age, gender, race, religion, marital status and family responsibilities, or disability.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for the technical R&amp;amp;D and quality breakthroughs of the runtime animation system for the dual-perspective shooting game, systematically improving character movement, aiming, weapon handling, combat states, and the overall shooting experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personally design, validate, and implement core solutions for aiming and weapon handling experience, procedural animation, animation graphs, and state orchestration. Identify and resolve animation quality issues across assets, engine, gameplay, and runtime from both first-person and third-person perspectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold decision-making authority for the project’s animation technical approach. Establish animation technical specifications, review standards, problem-diagnosis methods, and effect acceptance mechanisms. Drive stable mass production and continuous iteration of solutions within the project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with animation, programming, and game design teams to translate animation technical solutions into executable development plans and advance cross-team implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and mentor the animation TA team through matrix management, with authority to set team technical standards. Responsible for technical direction, coaching on complex issues, capability building, and experience accumulation, while enhancing the team’s ability to independently tackle difficult problems with project delivery as a priority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Many years of experience in game animation and animation TA R&amp;amp;D, having worked on top-tier high-quality realistic PvP shooter products. Experience in runtime animation development for Call of Duty PvP or equivalent-level shooting projects is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the feel and runtime performance of dual-perspective shooting games. Ability to independently take ownership of the design, R&amp;amp;D, and closed-loop delivery of one or more core systems, such as aiming and weapon handling, procedural animation, animation graphs, and state orchestration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete game development pipeline experience. Ability to independently drive targeted quality breakthroughs in runtime animation — from problem identification and technical validation to cross-team execution and live-operation effect evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Matrix-style technical leadership capability. Ability to set animation technical standards, break down R&amp;amp;D tasks, guide animation TAs’ professional growth, and lead the existing team to upgrade capabilities while prioritizing project delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Not limited to a single engine. Familiar with the runtime animation architecture of at least one mainstream or proprietary engine, and able to solve animation R&amp;amp;D problems using DCC tools, scripting, and toolchains. Experience with multiple engines is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in high-quality action game development, international project collaboration, or the ability to balance quality, performance, and maintainability in multi-character, multi-state, high-concurrency multiplayer scenarios is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use AI/Agents for animation data processing, R&amp;amp;D assistance, tool automation, problem analysis, or workflow efficiency improvements is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

